From 2f9b11ba9a8253160879f4130ccac4f17070f54c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden-Doris <doris@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:54:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Eden (Doris): real GPU barriers after compute and at
 wait-for-idle points after memory-writing draws

Eden only puts a barrier before a compute dispatch, and turns the game's "wait for idle" points into
an event wait with TOP_OF_PIPE as its destination and no memory barrier, which on Adreno guarantees
neither ordering nor visibility of earlier writes. Whether later draws then read unfinished culling
results, indirect arguments or vertex data depends on timing, and the speed-ups (a faster GPU thread
hands the GPU its work sooner) change the timing: Doris build 32 (speed-ups on stock Eden) brought
dark squares back on the ground although each speed-up gives the same results as Eden's code.
- After every compute dispatch, a barrier from the compute shader's writes to everything after it.
- At a wait-for-idle point after a draw that wrote storage buffers or images (or used transform
  feedback), a real full memory barrier; it ends the render pass as Eden's wait does.
- Every other wait-for-idle is Eden's, unchanged.
These only add synchronization (as Doris builds 6-29 did); what is drawn can only become more correct.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
